    "methodological_limitations": "Local Shapley attributions explain the ensemble_base_decision_margin (aggregated across 5 ensemble estimators) on the uncalibrated log-odds scale relative to the expected training baseline. Additivity holds strictly on this margin scale (output_margin = base_value + sum(shap_values)). Because Platt sigmoid calibration is non-linear, Shapley values do NOT additively sum to the final calibrated probability. Furthermore, Shapley values quantify statistical model behavior on observational data, NOT causal intervention outcomes. Changing a feature in reality will not causally alter churn propensity as estimated."
